  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want categories, topic lists and my flag buckets loaded from HFR's JSON API when it answers, with the HTML pages as fallback, so that lists load reliably and stay complete.\n\n### Scope\n\nA read-only HFRClient (ADR 0008) over `GET /webservices/rest_api.php?uri=<path>[&page=N&results_per_page=M]` (builder `HFREndpoint.rest`, LOT-041): categories, sub-categories, last topics of a category, one topic, and the flag buckets (`participated`, `read`, `favorites`). The JSON is decoded into the existing LOT-010 list models (DTOs stay internal). When REST fails or lacks a field, the client falls back to the HTML pages and the LOT-021/022/024 parsers. It reads with the account's session cookies and writes none back. Never `/posts/` (always 500). REST writes (POST/PUT) are out of scope.\n\n- Module: HFRClient · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium\n- Audit source: redface2 E1 (`docs/research/redface2-comparison.md:289`; its `PH:`/`ADR-003:` citations point outside this repository)\n- Legacy sources: none. The legacy app never called the REST API (no `rest_api` in francoisgn/hfrnow at `2440d79` nor in `origin/master`), so there is no legacy oracle for the JSON part. Facts come from HFR-PROTOCOL §7 (REST API row: JSON, hrefs `https://forum.hardware.fr/api/…`, 25 per page for topics, 20 categories) and redface2 E1 (`/api/…` hrefs 404 and are rewritten to `rest_api.php?uri=…`; `total_pages` = ceil(posts count / per page); `last_position` is an offset). The HTML fallback follows the LOT-021, LOT-022 and LOT-024 specs.\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-057-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-040 (#66, done)\n- LOT-041 (#67, done)\n- LOT-010 (#43, done)\n- LOT-021 (#49, done)\n- LOT-022 (#50, done)\n- LOT-024 (#52, done)\n- LOT-001 (#38, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged.\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model). The author must be a tier A model (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8).\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- `R57a` (categories), `R57b` (last topics of category 13), `R57c` (one topic) in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures/`: anonymous GETs, no oracle (no legacy code).\n- *Pending capture*: sub-categories (#285, cats 1, 2 and 10); the logged-in flag buckets `topics/{participated,read,favorites}` (no capture issue yet: open one, `host: mac`, `type: chore`, naming this lot); a page 2 or `results_per_page` answer; the 404 of an `/api/…` href (HFR-PROTOCOL: not tested). Never hand-build JSON and present it as HFR's (LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `R57a`-`R57c` decode into LOT-010 models; where the captures overlap, the result matches the HTML side (`R57a` against the LOT-002 oracle of `R01`: the same 20 categories).\n- [ ] Paging: `total_pages` = ceil(posts count / per page), default 25; `last_position` read as an offset, not a page; tested at the boundaries.\n- [ ] Every href is rewritten from `/api/…` to `rest_api.php?uri=…` and stays on the forum origin, scheme and host checked (LESSONS 37, 43); `/posts/` is never requested; no cookie is written back to the account.\n- [ ] Fallback: an HTTP error, invalid JSON or a missing field falls back to the HTML parser of the same list (mock transport tests); the rules are in the spec.\n- [ ] Flag buckets and sub-categories ship only with a capture; until then they are *pending capture* in the spec, and a partial PR says `Refs #83` with what is left.\n- [ ] No new public type in HFRModels without the core team's answer (core-model guard, EXTERNAL-AGENTS §3).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-057-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n### Old issue (frozen)\n\n[francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#85](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/85) — read-only history.\n\n### Status note\n\nEvery dependency is done on `dev-swift`; the `blocked` cell of `docs/LOTS.md` on 2026-10-27 predates that (orchestrator decision 2026-10-27).\n",
