   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-29) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`):\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/AGENTS.md): the rules and the definition of done (§9)\n- [docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md): claims, review and merge for outside contributors\n- [docs/agents/LESSONS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/LESSONS.md): the self-review table\n- [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md), [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md)\n- the LOTS.md row of this lot, and its dependencies: LOT-040 ([#66](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/66)), LOT-041 ([#67](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/67)), LOT-010 ([#43](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/43)), LOT-021 ([#49](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/49)), LOT-022 ([#50](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/50)), LOT-024 ([#52](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/52)), LOT-001 ([#38](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/38)), all done; also [ADR 0008](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/adr/0008-hfrclient-orchestration-module.md)\n\n**Spec:** you write `docs/lots/LOT-057-<name>.md` first (AGENTS.md §5 step 2), from this issue's scope, sources and acceptance criteria. The issue body is a stub, and the legacy app never used the REST API, so there is no legacy source and no legacy oracle: the sources are redface2 finding E1 ([docs/research/redface2-comparison.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/research/redface2-comparison.md), line 289; its `PH:`/`ADR-003:` citations point outside this repository) and the settled facts of [HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md) (line 420: `/api/…` hrefs 404 and are rewritten to `/webservices/rest_api.php?uri=…`, 25 per page, `total_pages` = ceil of the posts count per page, `/posts/` answers 500 so never call it). Captures that exist in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures/`: `R57a` (categories), `R57b` (last topics of category 13), `R57c` (one topic), all anonymous GETs. Gap: the authenticated flag buckets (`topics/{participated,read,favorites}`) and the subcategories endpoint have no capture, so those parts are *pending capture* (open a capture issue, `host: mac`, `type: chore`, naming this lot); the HTML fallback must reuse the existing parsers (LOT-021/022/024). If your DTOs need a new public type in HFRModels, stop and ask on the issue (core-model guard). The client reads with an account's session cookies and must not write cookies back.\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`, or `CLAIM REQUEST` if you have no write access (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §5). The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Opus → Fable (LOTS.md): the author must be a tier A model (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8). The adversarial review may be run by **another agent of yours**, as long as it uses a different model (AGENTS.md §6).\n\n**Merge:** if you have no write access, the steward merges after the APPROVE and green CI. Every lot delivered by an outside contributor is also listed for the final Fable audit (#326).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
